regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1098:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1099:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1100:#  *** #490 L4 -- READ THIS BEFORE THE BLOCK BELOW.  EVERYTHING IN IT WAS TRUE WHEN
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1101:#  #462 WROTE IT AND WAS EXPIRED BY #465 THREE ROUNDS LATER.  THE ROWS ARE SOUND; THEIR
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1102:#  STATED WARRANT IS NOT, AND A KILL CLAIM RODE ON IT. ***
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1103:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1104:#  THE CHRONOLOGY, from git rather than memory:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1105:#      7c9dd9e (#462)  wrote this block and its three-state model
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1106:#      4d05cf0 (#465)  "data and data_len were RELEASED APART" -- the fix for exactly
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1107:#                      the hazard this block describes
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1108:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1109:#  Post-#465 `free_data()` sets BOTH `d->data = NULL` and `d->data_len = 0`, and it is
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1110:#  `handle_command`'s prologue.  So:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1111:#    * the THIRD state below (`data == NULL, data_len STALE`) is NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE by
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1112:#      this route -- the session builds the FIRST state, both fields agreeing at zero;
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1113:#    * "handle_command ... NEVER resets d->data_len" is FALSE -- free_data resets it;
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1114:#    * "leaving data_len at the TOC's 408" is FALSE -- the prologue already zeroed it;
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1115:#    * and the M11 claim -- that swapping the guard to `d->data_len == 0` reaches
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1116:#      `memory_rw(..., NULL, 408, ...)` -- IS REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, not by argument.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1117:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1118:#  MEASURED 2026-08-28 (artifacts/gdromexitsix/opus_r2table_20260828/): the M11 mutant
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1119:#  built as a single line over the R2 fix, both trees run, results BYTE-IDENTICAL --
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1120:#      fixed:  alive=True  stale_says=1  stale_idle=0x0  Transfering=0
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1121:#      M11:    alive=True  stale_says=1  stale_idle=0x0  Transfering=0
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1122:#  M11 is EQUIVALENT.  No row can kill it because there is nothing left to kill.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1123:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1124:#  *** THE GENERAL LESSON, and it is the reason this is written out rather than deleted:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1125:#  A KILL RECORD IS TIME-INDEXED EXACTLY AS AN ABSENCE RECORD IS. ***  The carrier already
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1126:#  says an absence record must name its warrant and that any edit touching that warrant
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1127:#  RE-RUNS the death measurement.  The same holds for a claim that a mutant IS killed:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1128:#  #465 edited the warrant, and nothing re-ran the test for three rounds.  The block is
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1129:#  kept because its REASONING is still the right reasoning -- it is the WORLD that moved.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1130:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1131:#  What the rows below actually pin, stated correctly: the NO-DATA decline path, with
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1132:#  both fields at zero.  That is real, reachable, and worth a row.  It is simply not the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1133:#  third state.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1134:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1135:#  *** THE STATE THE FIX WAS WRITTEN FOR, AND UNTIL NOW NO ROW BUILT IT. ***
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1136:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1137:#  A seat observed that this detector sees `d->data` in TWO states and there are
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1138:#  THREE:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1139:#      never-allocated      data == NULL, data_len == 0     <- every nodata row
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1140:#      successfully-alloc   data != NULL, data_len == 408   <- the accept session
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1141:#      FAILED COMMAND       data == NULL, data_len STALE    <- nothing, until now
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1142:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1143:#  The third is exactly what this round's own motivation describes: a command
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1144:#  fails, `handle_command` frees `d->data` and leaves it NULL -- but NEVER resets
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1145:#  `d->data_len`, which is assigned in `alloc_data` and nowhere else.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1146:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1147:#  Why it matters beyond completeness: `if (d->data == NULL)` -> `if
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1148:#  (d->data_len == 0)` reads as a tidy-up (the guard tests one field while the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1149:#  body it guards uses another) and scores a CLEAN SWEEP on the 52-row table,
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1150:#  because in the only two states the table builds, both operands agree.  In the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1151:#  third state the mutated guard is FALSE and control reaches
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1152:#  `memory_rw(..., d->data /* NULL */, d->data_len /* 408 */, ...)` -- a
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1153:#  multi-kilobyte read from a NULL pointer.  The round's own defect class,
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1154:#  restored through a different door.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1155:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1156:#  CONSTRUCTION, and every constant is derived rather than guessed.  The data
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1157:#  port fills the packet LOW BYTE FIRST (`cmd[n] = idata; cmd[n+1] = idata >> 8`),
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1158:#  which is why the TOC staging writes 0x0014 to mean command 0x14.  So 0x2030
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1159:#  gives cmd[0] = 0x30 (read sectors) and cmd[1] = 0x20 (the ONLY data format
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1160:#  that does not itself exit).  cmd[8..10] stay zero, so sector_count is 0, and
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1161:#  OB-20's clamp rejects and `break`s BEFORE `alloc_data` -- leaving data_len at
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1162:#  the TOC's 408.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1163:t, alive, how = session(
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1164:    ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_CNTLO, "r8=0x98"] + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7])
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1165:    + ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_CNTHI, "r8=0x01"] + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x20)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1166:    + ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_COND, "r8=0xa0"] + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x40)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1167:    + ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_DATAP, "r8=0x0014"]
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1168:    + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7] * 6, CODE + 0x60)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1169:    #  second command: 0x30 / format 0x20 / sector_count 0 -> OB-20 rejects
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1170:    + ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_COND, "r8=0xa0"] + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x100)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1171:    + ["r7=0x%x" % GDROM_DATAP, "r8=0x2030"]
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1172:    + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x120)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1173:    + ["r8=0x0000"] + run([MOV_W_R8_AT_R7] * 5, CODE + 0x140)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1174:    #  *** #490 L4: THIS SAID "data is NULL, data_len is STALE" AND THAT STATE HAS NOT
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1175:    #  EXISTED SINCE #465. ***  handle_command's prologue is `free_data(d); /* #465 */`
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1176:    #  and free_data sets BOTH `d->data = NULL` AND `d->data_len = 0`.  Before #465 the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1177:    #  prologue cleared only the POINTER, which is why the original evidence for this
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1178:    #  row read `Transfering 408 bytes to 0x00000000` -- a pre-#465 artefact.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1179:    #  MEASURED, not argued: swapping the DMA arm's guard operand from `data == NULL`
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1180:    #  to `data_len == 0` is BEHAVIOURALLY EQUIVALENT -- both trees return
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1181:    #  `alive=True stale_says=1 stale_idle=0x0 Transfering=0`, byte for byte.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1182:    #  What the session actually builds is the NO-DATA state: both fields agree at
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1183:    #  zero, and the DMA arm declines on that.  The row is sound; its description was
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1184:    #  a wrong record.  (Found by the opus seat; the equivalence re-measured here
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1185:    #  rather than inherited, because a KILL record is time-indexed exactly as an
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1186:    #  absence record is -- #465 edited the warrant and nothing re-ran the test.)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1187:    #  arm correctly and trigger: data NULL and data_len 0 -- the no-data state
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1188:    + ["r7=0x%x" % (DMA + 0x0c), "r8=1"] + run([MOV_L_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x1a0)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1189:    + ["r7=0x%x" % (DMA + 0x14), "r8=1"] + run([MOV_L_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x1c0)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1190:    + ["r7=0x%x" % (DMA + 0x18), "r8=1"] + run([MOV_L_R8_AT_R7], CODE + 0x1e0)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1191:    + ["r1=0x%x" % (DMA + 0x18), "r2=0xa5"]
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1192:    + run([MOV_L_AT_R1_R2], CODE + 0x200) + ["print r2"])
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1193:row("nodata stale", "survived" if alive else "died", "survived",
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1194:    "FAILED-COMMAND state: data NULL, data_len 0 -- the fix's own path")
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1195:row("stale says", ("%d" % len(DMA_NOD.findall(t))) if alive else "died", "1",
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1196:    "and it declines by the NO-DATA arm, exactly once")
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1197:row("stale idle", printed(t, "r2") if alive else "died", "0x0",
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1198:    "+0x18 idle after the stale-length decline (0xa5 = the load never ran)")
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1199:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1200:#  *** #490: `stale quiet` RESTORES WHAT THE SIBLING FIX BLINDED, AND THE LOSS WAS MEASURED
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1201:#  BEFORE THE FIX LANDED RATHER THAN INFERRED AFTER. ***
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1202:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1203:#  The three rows above detect a mis-assembled packet only by the HOST DYING: each reads
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1204:#  `... if alive else "died"`.  Frozen and measured on the committed build, a packet with
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1205:#  cmd[0]=0x31 or cmd[1]=0x21 scored **55/58, CAUGHT** -- all three red, all via `died`.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1206:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1207:#  #490 de-fatalised both of those sites.  Re-measured against the post-fix binary with the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1208:#  SAME two packets: **58/58 BOTH TIMES** -- the triple reverts and this probe reads exactly   [58-row denominator, as measured then]
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1209:#  what a CORRECT packet reads.  Not merely vacuous: ACTIVELY MISLEADING, because a future
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1210:#  maintainer whose packet rots gets a clean run.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1211:#      artifacts/gdromexitsix/challenge_freeze_20260828/  (pre-fix, 55/58 twice)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1212:#      artifacts/gdromexitsix/blinding_20260828/          (post-fix, 58/58 twice)   [58-row denominator, as measured then]
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1213:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1214:#  *** THOSE ARE 58-row FIGURES AND STAY THAT WAY. ***  They are what the probe
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1215:#  measured when it had 58 rows; the gate pin is authoritative for TODAY's
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1216:#  denominator, and restating a past measurement in a later denominator is exactly
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1217:#  the frozen-number defect this project keeps correcting.  A score names the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1218:#  artifact that produced it, and these two name theirs.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1219:#
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1220:#  This row reads the DECLINE TEXT instead, on the session that is supposed to send a
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1221:#  CORRECT packet.  A mis-assembled one now reddens it whether or not the host survives.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1222:#  kills: a rotted test packet, and a deleted `case 0x30` (which would decline at default:)
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1223:#  via:   the two anchored decline regexes, which cannot fire on a correct packet
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1224:row("stale quiet", "%d" % (len(FMT_DECL.findall(t)) + len(CMD_DECL.findall(t))), "0",
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1225:    "the packet is well-formed -- NEITHER new site declines it")
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1226:
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1227:#  *** #490: THE DEATH-MODE ORACLE.  `how` has been threaded through 37 call sites since
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1228:#  ea97a10 and UNTIL NOW NO ROW READ IT -- that commit said so in its own message and the
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1229:#  plumbing stayed inert. ***  `alive` is False only when a read fails INSIDE a budget
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1230:#  window, so it is true of a HUNG emulator, a FROZEN one, and -- measured -- one already
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1231:#  killed after the last budget check.  `how` is the exit status and cannot be fooled that
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1232:#  way.
regress/gdrom_default_probe.py:1233:#  *** THE kills: LINE HERE READ "floor clause (b) -- reinstating either exit(1) at the
