codex
Two premises already need correction. Maple assigns only a local `odata`; it exits before copying that value to the caller’s buffer. The XScale `isteer` read is quiet, but its write arm exits on any nonzero value.

Maple also overwrites `dmaaddr` after a DMA transfer, beside another TODO questioning that update. I’m checking whether it is meant to remain the programmed start address; that could defeat ACCEPT even if an immediate write/read test passes.

