226:#       rows above, which already pass, would notice.
227:#   tail flags/r0/r1 -- the 0x30 counter exits on the subs BORROWING and owes
228:#       N alone (0x8); the registers pin #347's closed form on the borrow
229:#       path, which no earlier row covered. "tail V" repeats the run seeded
230:#       V=1: V must come back 0 on the borrow exit too (it is structurally 0
