241:#  #490: the two decline diagnostics the sibling round added.  ANCHORED on `-- declined`,
242:#  because the bare `unimplemented data format` also matches the upstream 0x24
243:#  warn-and-continue line -- measured, not assumed.
244:FMT_DECL = re.compile(r"unimplemented data format 0x[0-9a-f]+ -- declined")
245:CMD_DECL = re.compile(r"unimplemented command 0x[0-9a-f]+ -- declined")
246:
247:rows = []
248:
249:
250:#  *** THE ROW-NAME COLUMN IS 14 AND THE LONGEST NAME IS 12, WHICH IS NOT
251:#  SLACK -- IT IS THE DISCRIMINATOR. ***
252:#
253:#  gate_sh_rounding.sh counts rows with `^$v  .*ok$` -- TWO spaces after the
254:#  name.  Four names here are prefixes of others (`dma rd`/`dma rd x1`,
255:#  `dma rd`/`dma rdleak`, `dma alias`/`dma alias x1`, `scan`/`scan uniq`),
256:#  and they are unambiguous ONLY because %-14s leaves at least two spaces
257:#  after every one of them.  `dma rd` cannot match the `dma rdleak` row
258:#  because that row has an `l` where the pattern needs a space.
259:#
260:#  *** #490 L4: THIS SAID "13 or 14" AND 13 IS FINE.  THE LIMIT IS 13. ***
261:#  The format is `"%-14s %-12s ..."` -- a 14-column field PLUS a literal
262:#  space -- so the padding and that space add up like this, measured:
263:#
264:#      12 chars -> 3 trailing spaces   `^name  ` MATCHES
265:#      13 chars -> 2 trailing spaces   MATCHES  (the comment denied this)
266:#      14 chars -> 1 trailing space    UNSATISFIABLE
267:#
268:#  Found by the codex seat on #490's pass 1, which also caught that I had
269:#  copied the wrong bound ("<= 12") out of this comment and into a design
270:#  brief -- so the error had already propagated once before it was read.
271:#  The extra character is NOT slack to spend casually: at 13 the margin is
272:#  exactly the two spaces the gate needs, with nothing left over.
273:#
274:#  A row named 14 characters leaves fewer than two spaces and its
275:#  check becomes UNSATISFIABLE.  Checked, and this is the SAFE direction:
276:#  the count reads 0 against a wanted 1, so the gate fails LOUDLY rather
277:#  than quietly dropping the row -- the opposite of the padded-column trap
278:#  the carrier records, where a too-long name makes a row stop being
279:#  tested in silence.  Widen the column if a longer name is ever needed;
280:#  do not shorten the name to fit and leave the constraint unstated.
281:def row(name, got, want, note=""):
282:    ok = (got == want)
283:    rows.append((name, ok))
284:    print("%-14s %-12s %-12s %-34s %s" % (name, got, want, note,
285:                                          "ok" if ok else "FAIL"))
286:    return ok
287:
