web search: "273517" pdf "Interrupt" ...
codex
The registration check confirms that Maple uses `DM_DEFAULT`, so a debugger memory read can bypass its callback. Its oracle must observe a value produced by a guest load.

For XScale, `i80321_inten` is zero-initialized 32-bit state, and the interrupt controller points directly to that same field. That supports the read assignment, though the store path has a separate concern: it changes the enable mask without immediately recomputing the CPU interrupt signal.

