web search: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/a7b75c5a8c41445f33efb663887ff5f5c3b4454b/arch/arm/mach-iop32x/irq.c
codex
The exit census is five active `exit(1)` calls in Maple and eight in the ARM coprocessor file. None is wholly unreachable from guest execution. There is a narrower dead case: a PID read cannot reach the nonzero-PID exit in a continuing guest, because the only write that establishes a nonzero PID exits immediately.

The detector needs more than immediate readback: repeated reads to catch destructive behavior, a second stored value to catch stale returns, and a Maple check after completed DMA to test whether the stored address remains valid.

